date-released: 2026-11-25
abstract: "A static, permanent demo of an agentic AI prototype for supply chain risk management. A fictional electronics company receives news day by day, including a port strike at a key supplier. For each event the prototype reads the news, chooses a risk method (CVaR, VaR, mean variance, monitor or abstain), computes the risk with a deterministic engine, verifies the result, explains it and waits for a manager's decision. All numbers were computed in advance by the R risk engine included here, and text from the AI agents is replayed from recorded outputs. The page needs no server, language model or external service. All data is synthetic."
